      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T17:53:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can you look into `clock-bus \u003d \"NPCX_CLOCK_BUS_LFCLK\"` on pwm1?\ni see that used a lot on other boards.\nthe cros-ec equivalent seems to be `PWM_CONFIG_DSLEEP` and\ni remember we\u0027ve used that on previous boards to fix similar\nflicker issues.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "9b993284069e66a57971d1e1e79adfeb6deec915",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "995ba7d6_34822ea6",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/brox/jubilant/keyboard.dtsi",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106416
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T00:56:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure we can do this for ITE boards. Like https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/8b370f0c0d8950bd1e4e47f0195babc0dd064930/zephyr/program/brox/led_pins.dtsi#11, We used ITE boards which are not greater than 324 Hz. I added ITE to share more detail and check.",
      "parentUuid": "c54eb28e_b38d2fe5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "9b993284069e66a57971d1e1e79adfeb6deec915",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e812d4e4_44f85072",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/brox/jubilant/keyboard.dtsi",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1153134
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T03:56:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On Chrome EC OS, the PWM_CONFIG_DSLEEP flag makes pwm driver of ITE SOCs to select 32.768khz (stay active in low power mode) as clock source. Under the condition, maximum supported PWM frequency is 324HZ.\nOn Zephyr OS, if frequency property is \u003c\u003d 324HZ, the PWM driver will automatically select 32.768khz as clock source:\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/zephyr/+/refs/heads/main/drivers/pwm/pwm_ite_it8xxx2.c#146",
      "parentUuid": "995ba7d6_34822ea6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "9b993284069e66a57971d1e1e79adfeb6deec915",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
